alcedo (1.0.6-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Microsoft: personal Outlook.com accounts sign in through the browser with
    no setup. Work and school accounts still need their own client ID.
  * Microsoft: sending works when the account signs in with an alias, and sent
    mail is no longer filed twice in the Sent folder.
  * The activity log and error messages fully hide passwords that contain an
    @, and keep the host of a URL with an @ in its path or query.

